{"id":"mpa","corpus":"aws","title":"Multi-party approval","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/mpa/latest/userguide/what-is.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Multi-party approval"},{"kind":"p","text":"Security through approval"},{"kind":"p","text":"Multi-party approval is a capability of AWS Organizations that allows you to protect a predefined list of operations through a distributed approval process. Use Multi-party approval to establish approval workflows and transform security processes into team-based decisions."},{"kind":"p","text":"Figure 1: Diagram depicting the job functions for Multi-party approval."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Example scenario: Protect logically air-gapped vaults"},{"kind":"p","text":"You can use Multi-party approval with AWS Backup. AWS Backup offers logically air-gapped vaults, which are backup vaults with increased security features. For more information, see Logically air-gapped vault in the AWS Backup Developer Guide."},{"kind":"p","text":"When a logically air-gapped vault is protected with Multi-party approval, a request to create a restore access backup vault must go through an approval session. This means that the CreateRestoreAccessVault operation will require team approval before it can be executed. In Figure 2, this is represented with CreateRestoreAccessVault as the requested operation in the dotted box in a pending approval state. The approval session for the requested operation takes place in the approval portal."},{"kind":"p","text":"If the access request is approved, AWS Backup creates a restore access backup vault in the requester's account. This restore access backup vault is the requester's connection to the logically air-gapped vault. In Figure 2, this is represented with the requested operation in the dotted box moving from pending approval to approved."},{"kind":"p","text":"For more information, see How Multi-party approval works. To get started, see Set up Multi-party approval."},{"kind":"p","text":"Figure 2: Diagram depicting how Multi-party approval works. You can also use the AWS CLI & AWS SDKs instead of the AWS Management Console."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Required services"},{"kind":"p","text":"Multi-party approval requires AWS Organizations and AWS IAM Identity Center."}],"lemmas":{"multis":["multis","multi"],"parties":["party","parties"],"partying":["partying","party"],"approvals":["approval","approvals"],"securities":["security","securities"],"capabilities":["capability","capabilities"],"organizations":["organization","organizations"],"allows":["allows","allow"],"allowing":["allowing","allow"],"allowed":["allowed","allow"],"protects":["protects","protect"],"protecting":["protecting","protect"],"predefineds":["predefineds","predefined"],"lists":["list","lists"],"listed":["listed","list"],"listing":["listing","list"],"operations":["operation","operations"],"distributed":["distributed","distribute"],"distributeds":["distributeds","distributed"],"distributes":["distributes","distribute"],"distributing":["distributing","distribute"],"processing":["processing","process"],"processed":["processed","process"],"uses":["use","uses"],"using":["using","use"],"used":["used","use"],"establishes":["establishes","establish"],"established":["established","establish"],"establishing":["establishing","establish"],"workflows":["workflow","workflows"],"transforms":["transforms","transform"],"transforming":["transforming","transform"],"transformed":["transformed","transform"],"processes":["process","processes"],"teams":["team","teams"],"teamed":["teamed","team"],"teaming":["teaming","team"],"based":["based","base"],"baseds":["baseds","based"],"bases":["base","bases"],"basing":["basing","base"],"decisions":["decision","decisions"],"figures":["figure","figures"],"figured":["figured","figure"],"figuring":["figuring","figure"],"diagrams":["diagram","diagrams"],"depicting":["depicting","depict"],"depictings":["depicting","depictings"],"depic